{"name":"Lint","hex":"#adb28d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lint","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gossypium","blocks":[{"text":"Gossypium is a genus of flowering plants in the tribe Gossypieae of the mallow family, Malvaceae, from which cotton is harvested. It is native to tropical and subtropical regions of the Old and New Worlds. There are about 50 Gossypium species, making it the largest genus in the tribe Gossypieae, and new species continue to be discovered. The name of the genus is derived from the Arabic word goz, which refers to a soft substance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Gossypium_herbaceum_002.JPG/330px-Gossypium_herbaceum_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gossypium","wikidata":"Q719312"},{"title":"Lint (material)","blocks":[{"text":"Lint is the common name for visible accumulations of textile fibers, hair and other materials, usually found on and around clothing. Certain materials used in the manufacture of clothing, such as cotton, linen, and wool, contain numerous, very short fibers bundled together. During the course of normal wear, these fibers may either detach or be jostled out of the weave of which they are part. This is the reason why heavily used articles, such as shirts and towels, become thin over time and why such particles accumulate in the lint screen of a clothes dryer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Flusensieb_Trockner_02_%28fcm%29.jpg/330px-Flusensieb_Trockner_02_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lint_(material)","wikidata":"Q10815621"},{"title":"Lint (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Lint is a Unix utility that performs static program analysis on C language source code. The software gives its name to modern computing tools responsible for checking for coding style or formatting errors, known as \"linters\" or \"linting tools\", even though the original Lint program performed static program analysis."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lint_(software)","wikidata":"Q1727373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Gorskii_04431u.jpg/500px-Gorskii_04431u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Gorskii_04431u.jpg/1280px-Gorskii_04431u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Gorskii_04431u.jpg/500px-Gorskii_04431u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cotton field in Sukhumi Botanical Garden, photo circa 1912","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGorskii_04431u.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Baumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg/500px-Baumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Baumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg/1280px-Baumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Baumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg/500px-Baumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cotton field in Greece","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaumwollfeld_bei_Lagyna.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Cotton_plant_flower_G._hirsutum.JPG/120px-Cotton_plant_flower_G._hirsutum.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Cotton_plant_